  "body": "What happens: the 0.26.0 documentation site (branch `site/v0.26.0`, after 46957f4a7 for #3763) does not describe several things that 0.26.0 ships. A user cannot tell from the site that their control is supported, or that a known issue affects an option.\n\nMissing or thin, checked against `RELEASE_NOTES.md` of v0.26.0:\n1. New posts are not named anywhere in `site/content`: Mach3 Mill (#2482), Siemens Sinumerik 810M with the EMCO VMC-200 machine (#2888), the native Agie Classic Cut 2S job (#2945). No page lists the shipped posts by control. Add one list, for example in `guide/check-and-post/posting.md` or `guide/reference/post-processors.md`. Name each built-in post, its control and its machine files. Take the list from `assets/posts/` and `assets/machines/` at the tag, not from memory.\n2. \"Do not touch\" is new on Face, Trace, Engrave, 2D Adaptive and 3D Finish. The guide documents it on 2D Offset and 2D Pocket and mentions it once in the 3D page.\n3. Typed text as outline shapes: only the MCP row `insert_outline_text` mentions it. There is no guide section for the app.\n4. Known issues: \"Pass starts at\" Inside and Outside on 2D Offset give ramped linear cuts and lifts (#3741, now #3744-#3748). The guide documents the option with no warning. Add a short known-issue note that names the issues. It is removed when the fix ships.\n5. The upgrade notes are only in the release notes: project format 78 (older builds refuse it), part-off must be generated again before it posts (#3452), and the mm/inch question for a STEP file with no length unit (PR #3166). Check what the guide already says before adding.\n\nHow it ships: one docs-only PR into `site/v0.26.0` (base that branch, not main), so the maintainer can deploy it with release.yml's `site_only` dispatch. Then the same commits go to `main` in a second PR, so 0.27.0 keeps them. Run the site tests (`python3 -m unittest discover -s site/tests`, see `site/README.md`) on both.\n\nDone means: items 1-5 are in the site on `site/v0.26.0` and on `main`, the site tests pass on both, and the PR bodies list each item with its page.\n\nFollows #3763.\n",
